Package: txhome
Title: Explore How Texas Housing Markets Weathered the 2008 Financial Crisis
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Chenuli", "Muthukuda Arachchige",
           email = "cmut0005@student.monash.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides cleaned monthly housing market data for 46 Texas
    market areas from 2000 to 2015, including median prices adjusted for
    inflation, a function that summarises how far each market fell during
    the 2008 financial crisis and how quickly it recovered, and an
    interactive Shiny app for comparing the resilience of different
    markets. Housing data originally from the TAMU Real Estate Center, as
    distributed in the 'ggplot2' package; inflation data from the U.S.
    Bureau of Labor Statistics, retrieved from FRED.
